01:21:06,666 --> 01:21:12,666
A Cure for Wellness is a 2017 psychological horror film directed
by Gore Verbinski and written by Justin Haythe.

11
01:29:13,333 --> 01:29:19,333
Haythe and Verbinski were inspired by Thomas Mann's 1924 novel The
Magic Mountain while coming up with the idea for the film.

12
01:37:20,000 --> 01:37:26,000
Starring Dane DeHaan, Jason Isaacs, and Mia Goth, the plot follows a young executive who is sent to
retrieve his company's CEO from a mysterious rehabilitation center in the Swiss Alps.

13
01:45:26,666 --> 01:45:32,666
An international co-production based in the United States, Germany, and Luxembourg, the film was shot on
location at various German locations, including Hohenzollern Castle in Baden-Württemberg.

14
01:53:33,333 --> 01:53:39,333
A Cure for Wellness was released on February 17, 2017, by 20th Century Fox and received generally mixed reviews from critics, who
praised its visuals, cinematography, performances and ambition, but criticized its length, script and narrative.

15
02:01:40,000 --> 02:01:46,000
It grossed $26 million against its $40 million
production budget, making it a box-office bomb.

16
02:09:46,666 --> 02:09:52,666
The film explores themes of darkness, therapist,
switzerland, mountain, wellness.

17
02:17:53,333 --> 02:17:59,333
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
